 "note": "Buildings + goblin camp set + ruin. Points / footprints / collision boxes in Godot local coords (origin = ground at footprint centre of the main walls, front = +Z).",
 "convention": {
  "units": "metres, 1:1",
  "coords": "All points / boxes / sizes are GODOT LOCAL coordinates of the object: x = Blender x, y = Blender z (up), z = -Blender y. The model FRONT faces +Z (Godot Vector3.MODEL_FRONT); +X is the viewer's right when looking at the front (= the model's own left, Vector3.MODEL_LEFT). Origin = ground level at the footprint centre.",
  "facing": "facing = horizontal unit vector (Godot local). yaw_deg = degrees(atan2(facing.x, facing.z)); a character whose front is +Z faces that way with rotation.y = deg_to_rad(yaw_deg) (in the object's frame; add the object's yaw).",
  "vertex_color": "COLOR_0 (linear RGBA). A=0 fixed colour; A=1 tint mask (RGB = grey shade, multiply by instance tint: roofs/banners/awnings = civ colour, leaves/crops/vines = species/season colour); A=0.5 window glass (emissive at night).",
  "lod": "<name> = near mesh, <name>_lo = far mesh with the same silhouette (where provided).",
  "collision_boxes": "center/size in Godot local axes (size = [x, y(height), z]), yaw_deg about +Y. Use as BoxShape3D children of a StaticBody3D. walkable_boxes are floors/decks/steps a character may stand on.",
  "doors": "door points: pos = where a character stands just OUTSIDE the door (on the ground/deck), facing = the door's outward direction (the way you face when you come out). To enter, walk/face along -facing and fade out.",
  "seats": "seat points: pos = seat surface centre (character hips), facing = the way the sitter looks.",
  "footprint": "footprint = {center:[x,z], size:[x,z]} rectangle in the object's local XZ plane (flatten a terrain pad over it plus ~1 m margin). footprint_walls = the enclosed wall rectangle only."
 },
